      "term": "Zhenjiang Vinegar",
      "definition": "A dark, complex Chinese black vinegar with a smoky, mild flavour. Used widely in Jiangnan cooking. Balsamic vinegar diluted with a splash of rice vinegar is the best substitute."
    },
    {
      "slug": "cornflour-slurry",
      "term": "Cornflour Slurry",
      "definition": "A mixture of cornflour and cold water used to thicken sauces. Added at the end of cooking and stirred constantly until the sauce turns glossy and clear."
    },
    {
      "slug": "poaching-fish",
      "term": "Poaching",
      "definition": "Cooking fish gently in barely simmering liquid. The fish cooks in residual heat and stays tender. Boiling causes the flesh to break up."
